<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🧭 LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/surface_pressure/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Sea-level pressure (hPa, HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>LOWEST 980</b> dark-blue deep low &rarr; <b>1000</b> cyan &rarr; <b>1006</b> green &rarr; <b>AVERAGE 1013.25</b> yellow middle &rarr; <b>1017</b> orange &rarr; <b>1023</b> red &rarr; <b>1029</b> magenta &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 1040</b> dark-purple. Same pressure always shows the same color; the everyday average sits in the middle. Current basin range: <b>1013-1026 hPa</b> (above average (high)).</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km MSLMA mean sea-level pressure analysis (hourly cycles)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 10:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t02z-mslma-anl<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (hourly HRRR cycle)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🧭 LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Surface_Pressure.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
